  <section class="dorothy-copy" aria-label="About the project">
    <div>
      <h2>Evidence, not just answers</h2>
      <p>Claims connect to visible citations and source excerpts, so you can inspect what supports an answer instead of taking a polished paragraph on faith.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Research is a process</h2>
      <p>Questions lead into sources, comparisons, and synthesis. The interface makes room for uncertainty when the evidence is partial or the question asks for an interpretation.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>A colour constellation</h2>
      <p>Colour helps distinguish source identities and follow citation references through the page. It is a navigation cue, not a score for truth, trust, or certainty.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</article>
